@startuml fixed-delta-scaling-protocol
' ============================================================================
' The preregistered fixed-delta scaling experiment of task 7929 (pgmcp
' experiment 446), in the order it ran, with the amendments recorded before
' any decision data: A1-A3 (artifact 1173), C1, C2 and O2 (artifact 1178) and
' C3. The driver is scripts/bench/rspace-fixed-delta-scaling.py; the child is
' the ignored test scale_child in rspace++/tests/persistence/
' trusted_scaling_resource.rs; the idle rule is benchmark_host.cpu_snapshot.
'   INDIGO #283593  preregistration and the frozen protocol
'   AMBER  #EF6C00  feasibility: the pilots and the recorded amendments
'   PURPLE #6A1B9A  the negative controls, run first
'   TEAL   #00796B  the host guards before every attempt and every child
'   BLUE   #1565C0  the decision population
'   GREEN  #2E7D32  analysis, acceptance and durable records
'   RED    #C62828  outcomes that stop or invalidate a population
'   GREY   #607D8B  diagnostics, never pooled with timing data
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #455A64
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #455A64
skinparam NoteBorderColor #455A64
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #455A64

title <b>The fixed-delta scaling experiment, as it ran</b>\npreregistered before any sample; amendments may change only feasibility and order, never thresholds, metrics, arms, seeds or analysis

start
partition "preregister" {
  :open experiment 446 at commit 941ff07d:
  hypothesis, metric, criterion and protocol;<<#C5CAE9>>
  note right #E8EAF6
    <b>H1.</b> On each of U (<latex>N = 2^{10} \ldots 2^{18}</latex>, <latex>H = 2^{10}</latex>)
    and R (<latex>H = 2^{8} \ldots 2^{16}</latex>, <latex>N = 2^{12}</latex>), the per-commit
    thread CPU time of one-key replacements has a
    log-log exponent whose upper 95% bound is at most 0.25.
    The statistic is the larger of the two upper bounds.
  end note
  :build the release lib test binary from an export
  of the commit and pin it by its sha256;<<#C5CAE9>>
}
partition "pilots (never decide)" {
  :treatment pilot: each axis's extremes,
  1 verify run and 2 time processes per cell;<<#FFE0B2>>
  :amendments A1-A3: child timeout 7200 s; measure on CPU 2
  with other heavy jobs fenced away; a population interrupted
  by idle admission is rerun in full, at most three attempts;<<#FFE0B2>>
  :control pilots: one feasibility run of each control;<<#FFE0B2>>
  :addendum: C1 corrects NC-SCAN to revision r1; C2 runs
  the controls first; O2 forecasts the G4 allocation-byte miss;<<#FFE0B2>>
}
partition "controls (each its own population, run first)" {
  repeat
    :next control: NC-SCAN, NC-CLONE, NC-ORDER, then NC-V1;<<#E1BEE7>>
    :quiet wait (addendum C3, from NC-ORDER's fourth attempt on):
    the idle rule must admit 60 consecutive one-second snapshots;<<#B2DFDB>>
    :run the population: 5 processes, <latex>T = 8</latex>, at the
    smallest, middle and largest strata of U and R;<<#E1BEE7>>
    note right #F3E5F5
      NC-SCAN, NC-CLONE and NC-ORDER run release
      binaries built from mutated exports; NC-V1 runs
      the V1 writer on committed code. Every child
      passes the same per-child idle admission.
    end note
    if (interrupted by idle admission?) then (yes)
      :keep the partial population for the record (it never
      decides) and rerun in full in a new directory;<<#FFCDD2>>
      note right #FFEBEE
        NC-ORDER was interrupted three times. Addendum C3
        then confined this session's heavy jobs with taskset,
        restored the three-attempt budget and added the wait.
      end note
    else (no)
    endif
  repeat while (another control or rerun?) is (yes) not (no)
  if (G10: every control qualified and detected?) then (yes)
  else (no)
    :an undetected control invalidates the experiment;<<#FFCDD2>>
    stop
  endif
}
partition "decision population (21 cells)" {
  :quiet wait: 60 consecutive admitted snapshots;<<#B2DFDB>>
  :build each cell's fixture once
  (catalog, pack and index);<<#BBDEFB>>
  :two verify runs per cell: exact work, sealed objects,
  metadata, effects, files and ledger at every commit;<<#BBDEFB>>
  repeat
    :time-process round: every cell once,
    in an order shuffled with seed 7929;<<#BBDEFB>>
    :idle admission before every child: CPU 2 and its sibling
    <latex>\ge</latex> 90% idle and at least three physical cores more than half idle,
    from one-second mpstat snapshots, at most 30 tries;<<#B2DFDB>>
    :run the child under taskset on CPU 2, with the
    7200 s timeout, in a 16 GiB scope without swap;<<#BBDEFB>>
  repeat while (3 warm-up and 31 decision rounds done?) is (no) not (yes)
  :write the summaries, metadata.json
  and manifest.json;<<#C8E6C9>>
  :analyze H1 and G1 to G9;<<#C8E6C9>>
  if (qualified, and H1 and G1 to G9 pass?) then (yes)
    :the experiment is accepted;<<#C8E6C9>>
  else (no)
    :accepted = false: record each failing gate with its evidence,
    give a missed prediction a new hypothesis, and file a cost that
    grows with history as a bug item with a consensus-change assessment;<<#FFCDD2>>
    note right #FFEBEE
      Observed: H1, G1 to G3 and G5 to G9 pass;
      G4 fails on allocation bytes (H-O2).
    end note
  endif
}
partition "diagnostics (separate runs)" {
  :AMD uProf time-based sampling on the U and R extremes,
  heaptrack (record only) and strace -f -c on the U extremes;<<#CFD8DC>>
}
partition "records" {
  :archive every raw file as pgmcp artifacts with sha256
  values, under a top-level manifest;<<#C8E6C9>>
  :record the U and R upper bounds on experiment 446,
  finalize the run and decide;<<#C8E6C9>>
  :commit the summary files, the figures and the
  catalog, stack-safety and journal entries;<<#C8E6C9>>
}
stop
@enduml
